==Trivia==
*As mentioned in her Japanese description, Ururun is the name of the rider, not the wolf.
*This enemy was initially conceived as just a wolf, but art director Tamasan later added Ururun due to feeling that the wolf was [https://x.com/tamasanp/status/1839870225363415426 lonely].
*Ururun's clothing was very likely based on the female Kirin Armor from the ''[[wikipedia:Monster Hunter|Monster Hunter]]'' series.
**She could also be a reference to [[wikia:ghibli:San|San]] from the Studio Ghibli film ''[[wikipedia:Princess Mononoke|Princess Mononoke]]'', especially with her [[True Form]]'s red mask.
*Based on [[The Ururuvu Journals]]' Japanese name, Ururun was most likely named after the Japanese travel show [[wikipedia:ja:世界ウルルン滞在記|''Sekai Ururun Taizaiki'']] (世界ウルルン滞在記, "World Ururun Travelogue"), in which a TV personality has to stay with a local family abroad for a week.
*[[Urs & Fenrir (Special Cat)|Urs]] is potentially an ancestor of Ururun, as referred to in the ending of [[Stories of Legend]].
*Ururun and [[Kuu (Uber Rare Cat)|Kuu]] seem to be on poor terms with each other. [[Jungle Women (Combo)|Jungle Women]]'s Japanese name, Ken'en no Naka (犬猿の仲), literally translates to "Dog-monkey Relationship" and refers to a contentious relationship characterized by mutual hatred or extremely poor relations, like the rivalry between dogs and monkeys.
*According to [[Troubled Youth (Combo)|Troubled Youth]]'s Japanese name, Ururun and [[Akira (Uber Rare Cat)|Akira]] are examples of ''[[wikipedia:Chūnibyō|chūnibyō]]'' (中二病), a slang term essentially describing a delusional teenager (most commonly a 2nd-year middle-schooler) or young adult who tries to stand out through various stereotypical behaviors such as acting like a pretentious know-it-all, making believe they have special powers and/or pretending to be anti-social. This is further supported by [[Ururun Wolf (Special Cat)|Ururun Cat]]'s description, which states that she is delusional.
*The [[Hunting Club (Combo)|Hunting Club]] [[Cat Combo|Combo]] implies that Ururun is the "best friend who travels with a beast" mentioned in [[Terun (Uber Rare Cat)|Terun]]'s Japanese description.
*In The Ururuvu Journals, she appears with 300% HP and 500% attack power, making her the first enemy to use separate health and attack magnifications in a non-event stage.
*She is the first enemy unit to be unlockable as a Cat Unit.
*In a previous version of [[The Battle Cats]], she had the [[Ururun Wolf (Special Cat)|Cat Unit]]'s description instead, due to a bug.
*She is the final boss of [[The Battle Cats POP!]].

